================================================================================
Community detection at scale: label propagation on a Databricks job
================================================================================

Context:
Intelligence → Community → Detect failed or returned nothing on large domains
(e.g. Customers100M). Detection loaded every triple into the app and ran
NetworkX in memory inside a synchronous request: the triple guard only fired
after the full load, the request hit the Databricks Apps proxy timeout, and
detect / materialize / current all moved unbounded member lists between the
browser and the server. Detection now runs as semi-synchronous label
propagation in Spark SQL on a dedicated serverless Lakeflow job; the app reads
back bounded results, materializes server-side, and every heavy step is a
background task.

Changes:
1. src/jobs/graph_analytics_job.py — new `CommunitySQL` builder and
   `run_communities` stage runner (`--task communities`): portable LPA
   (md5-parity half updates, self vote, smallest-label tie break, stop after
   two quiet rounds or `--lp-iterations`), SQL modularity, and the outputs
   `graph_communities_<slug>`, `…_sizes`, `…_preview_nodes`,
   `…_preview_edges` (≤ 1,500 nodes / 5,000 edges) and `…_summary`.
2. resources/community_detection.job.yml — new bundle job
   `<app>-community-detection` (same script, max_concurrent_runs 1).
3. scripts/bootstrap/app-permissions.sh — grants CAN_MANAGE_RUN on both
   analytics jobs.
4. src/back/core/graph_analysis/LakeflowRunner.py — `submit_params`,
   `run_params_and_wait` and a configurable running label.
5. src/back/core/graph_analysis/JobCommunities.py (new) — triggers the job and
   reads its outputs with bounded queries (summary, top clusters ≤ 200,
   preview, member pages ≤ 500, keyset batches).
6. src/back/core/graph_analysis/CommunityMaterializer.py — rewritten:
   `INSERT … SELECT` from the job output on Delta, 50k keyset batches on other
   stores, clear on failure; bounded `load_current(limit)`,
   `assignments(uris)` (≤ 5,000) and `members(cluster_id, offset, limit)`.
7. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/MaterializedStore.py — new
   `insert_triples_from_select` writing into the inferred companion table.
8. src/back/core/graph_analysis/preflight.py, helpers/DatabricksHelpers.py —
   `community_job_status` / `community_job_configured` and
   `resolve_community_job_name`.
9. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinAnalytics.py — job wiring
   (`build_job_communities`, shared `analytics_output_schema`), detect on the
   analytics snapshot, latest / members / summary reads, materialize and
   bounded materialized reads.
10. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinBackgroundTasks.py — `run_community_task`
    and `run_community_materialize_task`; task failures keep the error detail
    (job run URL).
11. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py — detect and materialize return a
    task_id (preflight / "Run Detect first" → 400); new
    `GET /clusters/latest`, `GET /clusters/{id}/members`,
    `POST /clusters/assignments`; `GET /clusters/current` is top-N without
    members.
12. Removed `CommunityDetector`, `graph_analysis/GraphBuilder.py`,
    `ClusterRequest` / `ClusterResult` / `DetectionResult` / `DetectionStats`,
    the `analytics_max_triples` setting and `ONTOBRICKS_ANALYTICS_MAX_TRIPLES`;
    added `ONTOBRICKS_COMMUNITY_JOB_NAME`. The DigitalTwin cluster delegators
    were dropped (routes call TwinAnalytics / TwinBackgroundTasks directly).
13. src/front/static/simulation/js/simulation-communities.js,
    _sim_communities.html, simulation.css — Detect / Materialize run as
    tracked tasks (resumed on section open), single "Label propagation
    (Databricks)" algorithm, entity-type scope, inline preflight reason,
    run status line (rounds, convergence, Databricks run link), members paged
    on demand, Materialized panel rows expand to paged members.
14. src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js — Explorer reads totals from
    `/clusters/current` and looks up assignments for drawn nodes only.
15. tests/units/architecture/baseline.json — ratchet tightened; manual entry
    for `jobs/graph_analytics_job.py` (2 classes: the job script must stay a
    single standalone file on the Spark driver).
16. Docs — README, getting-started (env vars), user-guide, architecture
    (new "Detect on Databricks, then materialize" section), product,
    development, Sphinx graph_analysis page, help modal.

