--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Community job name: fall back from the analytics job name
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Context:
Locally, `.env` pins `ONTOBRICKS_ANALYTICS_JOB_NAME` because
`DATABRICKS_APP_NAME` is absent outside Apps. Community detection had no
matching pin and no app name to derive from, so preflight reported
"No Databricks job name could be determined" even though analytics was
configured. The community resolver now derives from the analytics job name
when both the explicit community setting and the app name are empty.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/helpers/DatabricksHelpers.py —
   `resolve_community_job_name` falls back by replacing `-graph-analytics`
   with `-community-detection` on the resolved analytics job name.
2. .env — `ONTOBRICKS_COMMUNITY_JOB_NAME=ontobricks-07x-community-detection`
   (local pin, parallel to the analytics job).
3. tests/units/core/test_helpers.py — `TestResolveCommunityJobName` covers
   explicit, app-name, analytics-fallback, and bundle-name drift.
4. docs/getting-started.md — documents the analytics-name fallback.

